{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Peter Prepares for Final Exams", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "A Whole New World", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 4, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 10, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.2", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Accurately use information about people's jobs and places of work in communicative situations", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"content": "The Sound /t/ Between Consonants", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "There are 4 different ways to pronounce the <span class=\"italic\">t</span> sound.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class =\"strong\">Sound 1: True t sound </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If <span class=\"italic\">t</span> is the first sound of a word or is the main sound of a stressed syllable, you say t like the actual t sound.  This rule overrules any of the other rules listed below. The <span class=\"italic\">t sound</span> is transcribed as /t/.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Examples: talk, attach, pretend, italics, started", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class =\"strong\">Sound 2: Quick d sound </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The <span class=\"italic\">t</span> is voiced and is pronounced to sound like a quick <span class=\"italic\">d sound</span> when it is between two vowel sounds.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Examples: daughter, computer, settle", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class =\"strong\">Sound 3:  A stop</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When the <span class=\"italic\">t</span> follows a vowel, <span class=\"italic\">n sound</span>, or <span class=\"italic\">r sound</span>, it becomes a <span class=\"italic\">stop</span>. The tongue moves up in the mouth to make the t but does not release.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Examples: partner, certain, fitness, wait", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class =\"strong\">Sound 4: Almost silent t</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The letter <span class=\"italic\">t</span> is sometimes almost silent when it follows an <span class=\"italic\">n sound</span> and is before a vowel sound or <span class=\"italic\">r sound</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Examples: center, gentle, advantage", "type": "text"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "programming ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the act or job of creating computer programs ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Are you learning computer programming?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le10ob04aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": " These are words you hear in a conversation about work.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to contribute ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to help to cause something to happen ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We have to contribute to online discussions.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le10ob04aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "overwhelming ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "difficult to manage ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: All this work is a little overwhelming.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le10ob04aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "tell me about it", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to agree with something ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Tell me about it! Working and going to school is hard.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le10ob04aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to retire ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to stop working at a job or career because of age", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I want to retire before I turn 60.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le10ob04aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"con